<title>USA: BOK Financial completes merger.</title>
<headline>BOK Financial completes merger.</headline>
<dateline>TULSA, Okla. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>BOK Financial Corp said Wednesday it completed its merger with First National Bank of Park Cities and Park Cities Bancshares.</p>
<p>The transaction was approved February 7 by Park Cities' shareholders.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, BOK Financial acquired the stock of Park Cities in an exchange for cash and notes. Park Cities Bancshares is a $226 million bank holding company with two locations in Dallas, Texas.</p>
<p>BOK president Stanley Lybarger said Park Cities will be the cornerstone of BOK's expansion into north Texas.</p>
<p>BOK is a two-bank holding company with $4.6 billion in assets. Its bank subsidiaries are Bank of Oklahoma N.A. and Citizens Bank of Northwest Arkansas N.A.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
